ed","year":2026},"UKR":{"name":"Ukraine","value":"Not banned","year":2026},"ARE":{"name":"United Arab Emirates","value":"Not banned","year":2026},"GBR":{"name":"United Kingdom","value":"Not banned","year":2026},"USA":{"name":"United States","value":"Not banned","year":2026},"VIR":{"name":"United States Virgin Islands","value":"Not banned","year":2026},"URY":{"name":"Uruguay","value":"Not banned","year":2026},"UZB":{"name":"Uzbekistan","value":"Not banned","year":2026},"VUT":{"name":"Vanuatu","value":"Not banned","year":2026},"VAT":{"name":"Vatican","value":"Not banned","year":2026},"VEN":{"name":"Venezuela","value":"Not banned","year":2026},"VNM":{"name":"Vietnam","value":"Not banned","year":2026},"WLF":{"name":"Wallis and Futuna","value":"Not banned","year":2026},"ESH":{"name":"Western Sahara","value":"Not banned","year":2026},"YEM":{"name":"Yemen","value":"Not banned","year":2026},"ZMB":{"name":"Zambia","value":"Not banned","year":2026},"ZWE":{"name":"Zimbabwe","value":"Not banned","year":2026},"_aggregates":{"Gaza Strip":{"name":"Gaza Strip","value":"Not banned","year":2026,"code":"PS_GZA"},"Kosovo":{"name":"Kosovo","value":"Not banned","year":2026,"code":"OWID_KOS"}},"_meta":{"title":"Bans on killing male chicks in the egg industry (chick culling)","what":"Legal status of culling newly hatched male chicks of egg-laying breeds. \"Not banned\" includes countries where no law was found (OWID: a country with no known law \"can safely be assumed to have no ban\"). The year in brackets in value is the year of the ban.","source":"Our World in Data, \"Banning of chick culling\" (Various sources, with major processing by Our World in Data)","url":"https://ourworldindata.org/grapher/banning-of-chick-culling","data_url":"https://ourworldindata.org/grapher/banning-of-chick-culling.csv?useColumnShortNames=false","licence":"CC BY 4.0. OWID FAQ: data marked \"with major processing by Our World in Data\" \"falls under our permissive CC BY license\".","licence_url":"https://ourworldindata.org/faqs","citation":"Various sources (2026) – with major processing by Our World in Data. “Banning of chick culling” [dataset]. Various sources, “Chick culling laws” [original data].","notes_from_source":"- Chick culling is the killing of newly hatched male chicks, which cannot lay eggs.\n- Hens that lay eggs come from different breeds than chickens raised for meat (called \"broilers\"). The male chicks of egg-laying breeds grow more slowly and give less meat than broilers, so raising them is not profitable.\n- Billions of male baby chicks are estimated to be killed around the world every year.\n- This data shows the legal status of chick culling, not how widely it is practiced.\n- Bans in Austria and France still allow the killing of baby chicks that are used as animal feed.\n- Bans prohibit killing chicks within the country, but not exporting them. After Germany's ban, male chicks have reportedly been transported to other countries where culling remains legal.\n- There is no EU-wide ban on chick culling. The European Commission has committed to proposing EU-wide rules to end the systematic killing of male chicks by the end of 2026.\n- The main alternative to chick culling is \"in-ovo sexing\", a technology that determines the sex of the embryo inside the egg, so that eggs with male embryos can be discarded well before hatching.\n- Ducklings are also killed soon after hatching in major duck-egg producing countries like China. No law specifically bans the culling of ducklings.\n- France's ban on chick culling explicitly excludes ducklings. In foie gras production it is the female ducklings that are killed, as their livers are less profitable.","processing_from_source":"Countries for which we found no law on chick culling are shown as \"Not banned\". Chick culling bans are notable legislative events that animal advocacy organizations track closely, so a country with no known law can safely be assumed to have no ban.","years":"Status as of 2026-09-01","count":246,"live":"Yes: ourworldindata.org grapher CSV sends Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *."}}